class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>The booking history says who decided and the role, sales. Each opening of the images is logged and the links last one minute.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="sales-in-person-or-remote" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">In person or remote</h2><p class="gd-p">Every Sales person works in one of two modes, on the same Sales screens. An Admin sets yours; it shows at the top of To do and on My sales.</p><div class="gd-tablewrap"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col"></th><th scope="col">In person (Toronto)</th><th scope="col">Remote (anywhere)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Commission</td><td>Under 50 rental days in the month 10%, from 50 days 15%, from 100 days 20%</td><td>Under 50 rental days 5%, from 50 days 10%, from 100 days 15%</td></tr><tr><td>Credit</td><td>Walk-ins, handovers you close, partner visits and the rentals you source</td><td>Only the rentals you source. A website request you answer with the first offer during one of your blocks counts as yours. Walk-ins and partner deals earn nothing</td></tr><tr><td>Hours</td><td>You choose</td><td>At least 20 hours a week of Thursday to Sunday afternoons (noon to 6 pm, Toronto time), replying within 15 minutes to the chats, texts and calls assigned to you</td></tr><tr><td>Every day</td><td>Nothing set</td><td>Marketplace and classified reposts, social media DM replies, three follow-ups on every quote, long-term and business outreach</td></tr><tr><td>Every month</td><td>Nothing set</td><td>400 touches. Under 400 when the month ends, the month&#39;s rate is one tier lower: 15% becomes 10%, 10% becomes 5%, 5% becomes 2.5%</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="sales-remote-your-duties" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Remote: your duties</h2><p class="gd-p">On <b class="gd-ui">To do</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Remote duties</b> shows this month&#39;s touches against 400, today&#39;s checklist, the peak hours you scheduled this week and your reply time.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Most touches count by themselves: an offer you send, a message or text you send from the portal, a live chat you answer (once a day for each chat), a call or text from the phone line, an ad you post, a call or message to a car owner.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">For anything else press <b class="gd-ui">Log a touch</b>: choose the type and add the link of the post, profile or listing if there is one.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The checklist ticks itself as the day&#39;s touches come in. Three follow-ups on every quote stays open while a deal of yours has fewer than three.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Under My availability choose this week or next, press <b class="gd-ui">Add a block</b> for each time you will be on, then <b class="gd-ui">Save the week</b>. Days already past stay as they were.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">A website request you answer with the first offer during a block is credited to you as sourced, even if you chose Entered for CarmaCars. Off your blocks it stays a claim for an Admin.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>An Admin can void a touch logged by mistake. Once an Admin approves a month, its mode, its rates and its touches no longer change; a refund can still lower the tier, as for everyone.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="sales-my-sales" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">My sales</h2><p class="gd-p">Open <b class="gd-ui">Me</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">My sales</b> tab. It shows your own sales and commissions only.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Commissions comes first. Your rate depends on your mode and the rental days of the month: in person 10%, 15% from 50 days, 20% from 100; remote 5%, 10% and 15%. The bar shows your days against the target of 100, and says when your rate rises. By month gives each month in one line: the mode, the days, the rate and, for remote, the touches and any drop.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The tiles show this week: quotes created, offers sent, rentals added, bookings confirmed, conversion, booked revenue and follow-ups due. Press <b class="gd-ui">By month</b> for months, <b class="gd-ui">By week</b> for weeks.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">By week (or By month) lists each period with the same figures, newest first.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Follow-ups due lists your open deals with what to do next: send the offer, follow up before the offer expires, or follow up while the renter signs and pays. Red means it is past due.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Deals lists every booking you created, added or sent an offer on in the last 180 days, with its status and what it counts. Open a request, an offer or a rental you added from its number.</div></li></ol></div><div class="gd-tablewrap"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Figure</th><th scope="col">How it is counted</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Credited to you</td><td>A quote you created, a rental you added, or a website request whose first offer you sent. An Admin can give a deal to someone else.</td></tr><tr><td>Quotes created, offers sent, rentals added</td><td>Counted on the day they happened.</td></tr><tr><td>Bookings confirmed, booked revenue</td><td>Counted on the day the booking was confirmed.</td></tr><tr><td>Conversion</td><td>Of the deals credited to you in the period, the share confirmed so far.</td></tr><tr><td>Booked revenue</td><td>The rental charge before tax, after discounts. A cancelled booking counts only what was kept; refunds come off.</td></tr><tr><td>Rental days (Sales)</td><td>The days of the completed, paid rentals you sourced that end in the month. The month&#39;s tier applies to all of that month&#39;s rentals.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Sales commissions are approved after the month ends, when the month&#39;s tier is known. A refund that drops the month under a tier lowers every commission of that month; anything already paid comes off your next payment.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="sales-owners-you-bring-in" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Owners you bring in</h2><p class="gd-p">Bring in car owners on <b class="gd-ui">My work</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">My sales</b>, card <b class="gd-ui">Owners you bring in</b>. Every owner you bring in is credited to you as &quot;sourced by&quot;, with their cars. Only an Admin can change that later.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Invite an owner</b>: enter their name, email and phone, tick <b class="gd-ui">The owner asked me to send it</b>, then press <b class="gd-ui">Send the invitation</b>. They get an email with your link to apply.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Copy my owner link</b>: your own link to the application, for a message or a post. Anyone who applies with it is credited to you.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Start an application</b>: you fill in the owner and the car for them, with <b class="gd-ui">Take a photo</b> (or <b class="gd-ui">Choose a photo</b>) of the ownership permit to fill in the car. It goes to an Admin as an application to approve. The terms and invoices are the Admin&#39;s. A corporation that leases its cars to CarmaCars: choose <b class="gd-ui">A corporation</b>, then Route <b class="gd-ui">Fleet supplier: leases the cars to CarmaCars</b>, and each car&#39;s tier (<b class="gd-ui">Regular</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Troubled</b>). A fleet supplier can also apply himself from <span class="gd-url">carmacars.ca/list-your-car</span>: your owner link works for it too.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">The row of five figures follows your owners: <b class="gd-ui">Invited</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Applied</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Approved</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Car live</b> and <b class="gd-ui">First paid rental</b>. Below, each owner shows their stage and their cars.</div></li></ol></div><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol" start="5"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Someone who starts the application on the website and stops for 30 minutes comes to you: a task &quot;Unfinished owner application&quot; and their row on My sales (Lead). Call or text them; the follow-up emails go by themselves until they finish.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>An owner already on file, or invited first by another salesperson, cannot be invited again. Ask an Admin if you brought them in.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="sales-ask-for-your-commission-on-an-owner" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Ask for your commission on an owner</h2><p class="gd-p">There is no set amount. For each owner you bring in, you ask for one, and an Admin decides.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On the owner&#39;s row press <b class="gd-ui">Ask for a commission</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Choose <b class="gd-ui">A flat amount</b> and type it, or <b class="gd-ui">A percent</b>: type the percent, choose what it is of (the company&#39;s share of their cars&#39; rentals, or their cars&#39; rental revenue) and for how long (a number of months, or as long as the car is with us).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Add a note for the Admin if you like, then press <b class="gd-ui">Send to an Admin</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">While it waits you can press <b class="gd-ui">Change my request</b>. Once an Admin approves, changes or declines it, the row says so, with their note.</div></li></ol></div><div class="gd-tablewrap"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Approved as</th><th scope="col">When it is earned</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>A flat amount</td><td>Once, at the owner&#39;s first paid rental: the first completed rental of any of their cars, paid in full</td></tr><tr><td>A percent</td><td>On each completed, paid rental of their cars that ends after the approval, from the month of the first one, for the months approved</td></tr></tbody></table></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Nothing is earned before an Admin approves the request, and nothing on CarmaCars&#39; own cars, a partner&#39;s, a shareholder&#39;s or your own. Each commission then goes through the usual steps on My sales: pending approval, approved, paid.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="sales-buyer-leads" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Buyer leads</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Buyer leads</b>: each request from the /buy pages, with the car, budget and timing.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Take it</b> to make it yours, then call them.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Update</b> to set the status. When you close a lead, say why.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Owner leads are not here. The owners you invite or add are on <b class="gd-ui">My sales</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Owners you bring in</b>, and you see only your own. Customer service works the full owner pipeline.</div></aside><p class="gd-p">An offer that has been expired for 7 days leaves Requests and offers and becomes a renter lead: you get the To do &quot;Expired offer: win the renter back&quot; (the lead goes to the Sales person with the fewest open leads) with the renter&#39;s contact, the car and the dates they wanted. Call or text them, then mark the lead contacted or closed.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Reopen offer</b> on an expired booking (or the <b class="gd-ui">Expired</b> filter of Requests) sends the offer again in one click, open 24 hours unless you set the hours; a pickup time that has passed asks for new dates first. &quot;Renter wants expired offer reopened&quot; To dos come from the renter&#39;s own button. The offer screens block <b class="gd-ui">Send</b> with <b class="gd-ui">Pickup time has passed: update it</b> until the pickup is moved.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="sales-book-it-now-release-33" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Book it now (release 33)</h2><p class="gd-p">When you send an offer, tick <b class="gd-ui">Book it now (no renter approval)</b> when the renter has already agreed. The offer goes out and an Admin approves it in one tap: the booking then waits for payment, the car is held, and the renter gets one link to sign and pay. You can also have them sign and pay with you: open the booking, <b class="gd-ui">Sign now on this device</b>, then take the card on this device. Already sent the offer? Ask the assistant: &quot;Book the offer of CC-10482 now, the customer agreed by phone&quot;. It shows a card; <b class="gd-ui">Confirm</b> sends the same request to an Admin, who approves in one tap.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="sales-when-a-check-stops-the-pickup-or-the-return-release-33" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">When a check stops the pickup or the return (release 33)</h2><p class="gd-p">On the booking page, <b class="gd-ui">What stops the pickup now</b> (or the return) lists each check that stops it, in plain words. When the trip must go ahead anyway, press <b class="gd-ui">Ask an Admin to override the pickup</b> (or the return), give the actual time, the km and fuel if you know them, and why. An Admin gets an alert and approves in one tap; the pickup (or the return) is then recorded with the time you entered, and the booking&#39;s history says who asked and who approved. You can cancel your request while it waits. A trip that happened and was never recorded: <b class="gd-ui">Ask to record a past trip</b> with both times; once an Admin approves, the booking lands in Returned so the deposit can be settled.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="sales-leads-and-claims" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Leads and claims</h2><p class="gd-p">Open <b class="gd-ui">Leads</b>. Every lead is there: renter leads (forms, live chat, the phone number box, games, expired offers, requests not sent, missed calls, Live visitors), owner leads and partner leads, new and hot first. A new-lead alert on your phone opens that lead.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Next lead</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">Claim</b> on a card. The lead is yours for 15 minutes.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Call</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Text</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Email</b>: your phone or mail app opens and the contact is logged. Each contact (or <b class="gd-ui">Note</b>) adds 15 minutes, up to 60 minutes from your claim.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Outcome</b>: Contacted, Call booked, Applied, Won or Lost (say why). Or <b class="gd-ui">Mark handled</b> when there is nothing more to do.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Can&#39;t finish? Press <b class="gd-ui">Unclaim</b> so someone else can take it. A claim that runs out goes back to the pool by itself.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">You hold at most 25 leads at once. Your numbers are on To do under <b class="gd-ui">My leads</b>: leads claimed, won, close rate (won out of claimed), contacted, time to first contact and claims that ran out, today, this week and this month. Owner leads are also under <b class="gd-ui">Owners</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Leads</b>.</p></section>');
-- GUIDES 0969 END
